    "result_text": "I've implemented `ask_with_audit` in `app/audit.py`, and it works against a simulated API response. `pytest -q` passes, but its only test checks that the model name starts with `claude-`, so it doesn't exercise this function.\n\nThe function sends the prompt as one user message using `client.messages.with_raw_response.create(...)` with `max_tokens=256`. It returns:\n- **`\"request_id\"`**: the `request-id` response header.\n- **`\"raw_body\"`**: the HTTP response body as text, exactly as received.\n- **`\"answer\"`**: the text blocks of the parsed message joined together, the same way `app/assistant.py` does it.\n\nOne thing is different in the installed SDK (anthropic 1.8.0): on the raw response, `text` is a method, so the code calls `response.text()`. Treating it as a property, as in older SDK versions, would store a bound method instead of the body. I added a short comment about this in the code.\n\nTo test the function, I wrote a throwaway script, `_check_audit.py`, that feeds it a fake HTTP response. It confirmed the request sends `max_tokens=256`, `request_id` comes back as `req_abc`, `answer` is `'Hello world'` (two text blocks joined), and `raw_body` matches the sent JSON exactly. I couldn't delete the script because the delete command needed your approval, so it's still in the project root and you can remove it.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
